  <h2>Use it in real life</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>From home to work:</b> Give the teacher walking or driving directions from your home to your work or a favorite store. <span class="ex">Go straight on my street, turn right at the light, and go past the school.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Describe your street:</b> Say what is on your street and where each place sits. <span class="ex">There’s a small store next to my building. The bus stop is across from the park.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Ask the teacher:</b> The teacher chooses a place in their town. Ask politely, listen to the directions, and thank them. <span class="ex">Excuse me, how do I get to the museum from here? … Thanks so much!</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Your favorite place:</b> Name your favorite place in town, say why you like it, and explain how to get there from your home.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Plan a visitor’s afternoon:</b> A friend is visiting your city for one afternoon. Choose three places and give directions from one to the next. <span class="ex">Start at the museum. From there, go straight two blocks to the park…</span></div>

  <h2>Reflect</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Explain the system</h3>
    <p>Complete this aloud: “To give directions, I start with a verb: ______, go, take. To say where a place sits, I use chunks like next to, ______, between, and on the corner of. To ask a stranger politely, I open with ______, and when someone thanks me, I say ______.”</p>
    <p>Then give one real direction: how do you get from where you are sitting right now to the nearest store?</p>
  </div>

